==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{der|is|non|heill}} (compare {{cog|fo|heilur}}, Norwegian, Danish, and Swedish {{m|da|hel}}), from {{der|is|gem-pro|*hailaz}} (compare {{cog|en|whole}}, {{m|en|hale}}, {{cog|nl|heel}}, {{cog|de|heil}}), from {{der|is|ine-pro|*kóh₂ilus||healthy, whole}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/heitl/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|eitl}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|heilli|heilastur}}

# [[healthy]]
#* [[w:en:Hávamál|Hávamál]] ([[s:en:Poetic Edda/Hávamál|English source]], [[s:is:Hávamál|Icelandic source]])
#*: ''Gefendur '''heilir'''!''
#*: ''Gestur er inn kominn!''
#*: ''hvar skal sitja sjá?''
#*: ''Mjög er bráður''
#*: ''sá er á bröndum skal''
#*: ''síns um freista frama.''
#*:: '''Hail''' to the giver! | a guest has come;
#*:: Where shall the stranger sit?
#*:: Swift shall he be who, | with swords shall try
#*:: The proof of his might to make.
# [[complete]], [[entire]], [[whole]]
#: ''Þetta tók '''heilt''' ár!''
#:: This took a '''whole''' year!
# [[undamaged]], [[in one piece]]

